<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Expedition of the Thousand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Spedizione dei Mille</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Expedition of the Thousand was the campaign led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a> in 1860, in which about a thousand volunteers in red shirts sailed from near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marsala">Marsala</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in May. They defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> forces, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> and crossed to the mainland, entering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> in September. The fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</a> opened the way for the proclamation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> in 1861.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand.jpg" alt="Expedition of the Thousand" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Partenza_da_Quarto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
